WEBVTT

1
00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:32.791
<b>  </b>

2
00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:35.791
<b>Dhritarashtra's first question was, </b>

3
00:01:35.791 --> 00:01:37.083
<b>"O Sanjay,</b>

4
00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:43.708
<b>what did my sons and the sons of Pandu</b>
<b>do on the sacred battlefield of Kurukshetra?"</b>

5
00:01:43.708 --> 00:01:50.333
<b>Sanjay, in response to the question and observing</b>
<b>Dhritarashtra's anxiety for his sons, </b>

6
00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:56.125
<b>first focused on Duryodhana and presented</b>
<b>the Kaurava perspective.</b>

7
00:01:56.125 --> 00:01:56.875
<b>Now, </b>

8
00:01:56.875 --> 00:02:00.541
<b>Sanjay turns his gaze to the Pandava side</b>

9
00:02:00.541 --> 00:02:01.666
<b>and narrates:</b>

10
00:02:01.666 --> 00:02:04.333
<b>After the Kauravas' conch shells sounded, </b>

11
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:07.791
<b>Seated in a grand chariot drawn by white horses, </b>

12
00:02:07.791 --> 00:02:09.458
<b>Lord Krishna and Arjuna, </b>

13
00:02:09.458 --> 00:02:12.166
<b> blew their divine conches.</b>

14
00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:14.750
<b>Lord Krishna sounded His conch</b>
<b>called Panchajanya, </b>

15
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.833
<b>Arjuna blew his Devadatta, </b>

16
00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:18.833
<b>And the voracious eater, Bhima, </b>

17
00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:21.500
<b>blew his mighty conch horn called Paundra.</b>

18
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.583
<b>Kunti's son,</b>

19
00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:24.250
<b>King Yudhishthira, </b>

20
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:25.791
<b>blew the Anantavijaya, </b>

21
00:02:25.791 --> 00:02:28.500
<b>while Nakula and Sahadeva blew the </b>

22
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.791
<b>Sughosha and Manipushpaka</b>
<b>conch respectively. </b>

23
00:02:32.791 --> 00:02:38.583
<b>Sanjay continues, addressing Dhritarashtra, </b>

24
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:40.875
<b>"O Emperor of the Earth, </b>

25
00:02:40.875 --> 00:02:44.041
<b>the great archer, the King of Kashi, </b>

26
00:02:44.041 --> 00:02:45.583
<b>the mighty warrior Shikhandi, </b>

27
00:02:45.583 --> 00:02:46.791
<b>Dhrishtadyumna, </b>

28
00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:48.041
<b>King Virata, </b>

29
00:02:48.041 --> 00:02:50.500
<b>the unconquerable Satyaki, </b>

30
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.875
<b>King Drupada, </b>

31
00:02:51.875 --> 00:02:53.708
<b>the sons of Draupadi, </b>

32
00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:56.375
<b>and the strong-armed</b>
<b>son of Subhadra, Abhimanyu </b>

33
00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:59.750
<b>all blew their respective conches."</b>

34
00:03:00.416 --> 00:03:04.625


35
00:03:04.625 --> 00:03:09.750
<b>This marks the first appearance</b>
<b>of Lord Krishna in the Gita,</b>

36
00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:14.000
<b>albeit in the humble role of a charioteer.</b>

37
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.625
<b>Though Krishna's position is that of a charioteer, </b>

38
00:03:17.625 --> 00:03:21.500
<b>Though Krishna's position is that</b>
<b>of a charioteer Sanjay mentions Him first, </b>

39
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.041
<b>addressing Him as Madhava </b>

40
00:03:25.041 --> 00:03:29.541
<b>Madhava - meaning the Lord of Fortune,</b>
<b>the consort of Goddess Lakshmi.</b>

41
00:03:29.541 --> 00:03:32.458
<b>Sanjay also calls Him Hrishikesha </b>

42
00:03:32.458 --> 00:03:36.208
<b>Hrishikesha – the Master of the Senses.</b>

43
00:03:36.208 --> 00:03:38.625
<b>You might have noticed </b>

44
00:03:38.625 --> 00:03:44.166
<b>that when Duryodhana spoke of the</b>
<b>Pandava army, he didn't even mention Krishna,</b>

45
00:03:44.166 --> 00:03:48.416
<b>for in his eyes, what could a mere charioteer do?</b>

46
00:03:48.416 --> 00:03:51.375
<b>Before the war, when given a choice </b>

47
00:03:51.375 --> 00:03:55.750
<b>between Krishna Himself or His vast army, </b>

48
00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.166
<b>Duryodhana was overjoyed to choose the army. </b>

49
00:03:59.166 --> 00:04:01.458
<b>He valued only physical strength.</b>

50
00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:02.541
<b>However, </b>

51
00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:08.166
<b>Arjuna, felt blessed to have Krishna by his side. </b>

52
00:04:08.166 --> 00:04:12.875
<b>Sanjay refers to Arjuna as Dhananjaya </b>

53
00:04:12.875 --> 00:04:17.333
<b>Dhananjaya – the conqueror of</b>
<b>wealth and prosperity. </b>

54
00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:22.041
<b>Yudhishthira is respectfully addressed as King. </b>

55
00:04:22.041 --> 00:04:24.541
<b>Bhima is called Vrikodara </b>

56
00:04:24.541 --> 00:04:28.375
<b>the one with a wolf-like appetite and might.</b>

57
00:04:28.375 --> 00:04:35.583
<b>Sanjay's respectful mention of Duryodhana's</b>
<b>enemies in front of Dhritarashtra</b>

58
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:38.041
<b>This clearly shows </b>

59
00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:43.875
<b>his reverence for Krishna and the Pandavas. </b>

60
00:04:43.875 --> 00:04:47.333
<b>He also understands</b>

61
00:04:47.333 --> 00:04:53.750
<b>and foresees that this war will be</b>
<b>disastrous for the Kauravas. </b>

62
00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:57.458
<b>So why can't King Dhritarashtra comprehend this?</b>

63
00:04:57.458 --> 00:04:59.916
<b>Unable to contain his inner turmoil, </b>

64
00:04:59.916 --> 00:05:04.125
<b>Sanjay addresses Dhritarashtra as</b>
<b>"O Emperor of the Earth," </b>

65
00:05:04.125 --> 00:05:08.625
<b>as if to say, "Dhritarashtra,</b>
<b>you're the emperor of this land, </b>

66
00:05:08.625 --> 00:05:10.583
<b>of your people, </b>

67
00:05:10.583 --> 00:05:12.458
<b>of the Kauravas. </b>

68
00:05:12.458 --> 00:05:14.125
<b>  Why don't you stop this</b>

69
00:05:14.125 --> 00:05:16.166
<b>impending destruction?"</b>

70
00:05:16.166 --> 00:05:17.666
<b>Alas, </b>

71
00:05:17.666 --> 00:05:21.958
<b>the eyes of Dhritarashtra's mind are also blind.</b>

72
00:05:22.541 --> 00:05:26.666


73
00:05:26.666 --> 00:05:28.500
<b>In the war, </b>

74
00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.166
<b>when the proclamation from the</b>

75
00:05:32.166 --> 00:05:34.708
<b>From the Pandava’s side,</b>

76
00:05:34.708 --> 00:05:36.958
<b>I was the first</b>

77
00:05:36.958 --> 00:05:39.708
<b>to pick up the Panchajanya conch, </b>

78
00:05:39.708 --> 00:05:43.000
<b>and make a terrible blast. </b>

79
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.375
<b>I was leading the Pandavas.</b>

80
00:05:48.375 --> 00:05:51.500
<b>An ordinary charioteer, </b>

81
00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:55.583
<b>whom Duryodhana had completely ignored. </b>

82
00:05:55.583 --> 00:05:58.291
<b>He was overjoyed </b>

83
00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:01.666
<b>when I gave him my vast army. </b>

84
00:06:01.666 --> 00:06:03.083
<b>He thought,</b>

85
00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:06.125
<b>where is this mighty army, </b>

86
00:06:06.125 --> 00:06:09.458
<b>and where am I unarmed. </b>

87
00:06:09.458 --> 00:06:11.208
<b>He had spent his whole life </b>

88
00:06:11.208 --> 00:06:14.791
<b>in the race to accumulate power, </b>

89
00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:15.875
<b>so now </b>

90
00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:21.625
<b>he could only see the strength</b>
<b>of the body and weapons. </b>

91
00:06:21.625 --> 00:06:23.083
<b>My power </b>

92
00:06:23.083 --> 00:06:25.041
<b>resides not only in might </b>

93
00:06:25.041 --> 00:06:26.291
<b>but also </b>

94
00:06:26.291 --> 00:06:28.791
<b> in a clear mind.</b>

95
00:06:28.791 --> 00:06:30.250
<b>The power</b>

96
00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:34.291
<b>that the Pandavas possess.</b>

97
00:06:34.291 --> 00:06:36.458
<b>So you tell me, </b>

98
00:06:36.458 --> 00:06:39.583
<b>are you Duryodhana</b>

99
00:06:39.583 --> 00:06:42.333
<b> or Arjuna?</b>

100
00:06:42.333 --> 00:06:47.250
<b>In the pursuit of material pleasure and wealth,</b>

101
00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.458
<b>have you forgotten your dharma? </b>

102
00:06:50.458 --> 00:06:51.875
<b>The power of a pure mind</b>

103
00:06:51.875 --> 00:06:56.541
<b>established in dharma is unparalleled. </b>

104
00:06:56.541 --> 00:06:59.625
<b> It gives you immense strength. </b>

105
00:06:59.625 --> 00:07:02.625
<b>Provides mental balance, </b>

106
00:07:02.625 --> 00:07:04.708
<b>and with all this, </b>

107
00:07:04.708 --> 00:07:06.791
<b>you can achieve </b>

108
00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:09.458
<b>what you want.</b>

109
00:07:09.458 --> 00:07:12.916
<b>Just keep this mind pure, </b>

110
00:07:12.916 --> 00:07:17.458
<b>fame and wealth will come on their own.</b>

111
00:07:17.458 --> 00:07:19.333
<b>So friends, </b>

112
00:07:19.333 --> 00:07:21.541
<b>in this Mahabharata of life, </b>

113
00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:25.916
<b>whom will you choose as your charioteer? </b>

114
00:07:25.916 --> 00:07:28.500
<b>My army? </b>

115
00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:30.166
<b>Or me?</b>

116
00:07:30.708 --> 00:07:34.625


117
00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:39.791
<b>The five Pandava brothers</b>
<b>had completely different personalities. </b>

118
00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:42.958
<b>Sometimes like night and day. </b>

119
00:07:42.958 --> 00:07:44.791
<b>Where Yudhishthira</b>

120
00:07:44.791 --> 00:07:46.916
<b>worked with peace, </b>

121
00:07:46.916 --> 00:07:49.875
<b>Bhima, in complete contrast, </b>

122
00:07:49.875 --> 00:07:53.000
<b>would get fierce at every point. </b>

123
00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.583
<b>But still, </b>

124
00:07:54.583 --> 00:07:57.083
<b>the five were united. </b>

125
00:07:57.083 --> 00:07:59.916
<b>Like the five fingers of a hand </b>

126
00:07:59.916 --> 00:08:03.333
<b>that are different in length and strength </b>

127
00:08:03.333 --> 00:08:09.875
<b>but together form the strength of a fist.</b>

128
00:08:09.875 --> 00:08:13.666
<b>  The members of a family also</b>

129
00:08:13.666 --> 00:08:16.250
<b>  have different natures. </b>

130
00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:17.791
<b>Some are mischievous,   </b>

131
00:08:17.791 --> 00:08:19.166
<b> some are calm. </b>

132
00:08:19.166 --> 00:08:20.250
<b>Some are cool, </b>

133
00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:21.833
<b>some are hot.   </b>

134
00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:23.833
<b>Flowers of different kinds,   </b>

135
00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:26.666
<b>each with its own color,  </b>

136
00:08:26.666 --> 00:08:29.416
<b>each with its own fragrance, </b>

137
00:08:29.416 --> 00:08:30.541
<b>but </b>

138
00:08:30.541 --> 00:08:36.125
<b>when an outsider looks at such a</b>
<b>garden of flowers, </b>

139
00:08:36.125 --> 00:08:38.208
<b>he derives joy, </b>

140
00:08:38.208 --> 00:08:40.625
<b>he smiles. </b>

141
00:08:40.625 --> 00:08:45.416
<b>The family is also such a garden.</b>

142
00:08:45.416 --> 00:08:48.708
<b>All that is needed are some</b>
<b>responsible gardeners. </b>

143
00:08:48.708 --> 00:08:52.916
<b>Who keep watering with the water of</b>
<b>truth from time to time,</b>

144
00:08:52.916 --> 00:08:55.333
<b>keep adding the manure of knowledge, </b>

145
00:08:55.333 --> 00:09:00.541
<b>keep tending the flowers with their pure hands.  </b>

146
00:09:00.541 --> 00:09:08.083
<b>The elders of the house are the gardeners</b>
<b>who nurture this family garden.  </b>

147
00:09:08.083 --> 00:09:10.791
<b>As the elders of the family, </b>

148
00:09:10.791 --> 00:09:14.125
<b>if you keep your mind pure, </b>

149
00:09:14.125 --> 00:09:17.666
<b>keep acquiring knowledge yourself, </b>

150
00:09:17.666 --> 00:09:23.958
<b>then by sharing all this, you will be able to</b>

151
00:09:23.958 --> 00:09:26.291
<b>Take from me, </b>

152
00:09:26.291 --> 00:09:28.000
<b>the wealth of wisdom, </b>

153
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.166
<b>the treasure of knowledge. </b>

154
00:09:30.166 --> 00:09:32.333
<b>In the Gita, there are not words, </b>

155
00:09:32.333 --> 00:09:35.083
<b>but diamonds and pearls scattered. </b>

156
00:09:35.083 --> 00:09:39.291
<b>For you.</b>

157
00:09:39.291 --> 00:09:41.958
<b>Under these teachings of the Gita, </b>

158
00:09:41.958 --> 00:09:44.250
<b>there is the shade of dharma, </b>

159
00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.541
<b>in which elders, </b>

160
00:09:45.541 --> 00:09:46.833
<b>youngsters, </b>

161
00:09:46.833 --> 00:09:50.250
<b>all can come together, </b>

162
00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:53.708
<b>all will be benefited.</b>

163
00:09:54.291 --> 00:09:58.458


164
00:09:58.458 --> 00:10:01.875
<b>People under your leadership, </b>

165
00:10:01.875 --> 00:10:05.541
<b>are they eager to follow you? </b>

166
00:10:05.541 --> 00:10:09.458
<b>Or are the poor compelled?</b>

167
00:10:09.458 --> 00:10:12.500
<b>When Arjuna got a chance to choose, </b>

168
00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:16.375
<b>he did not even look towards my powerful army, </b>

169
00:10:16.375 --> 00:10:18.250
<b>without hesitation, </b>

170
00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:21.250
<b>he demanded to be with me. </b>

171
00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:26.166
<b>He saw true guidance in me, </b>

172
00:10:26.166 --> 00:10:28.666
<b>he saw affection in me </b>

173
00:10:28.666 --> 00:10:33.083
<b>and I in him.</b>

174
00:10:33.083 --> 00:10:36.791
<b>Will your people choose you </b>

175
00:10:36.791 --> 00:10:39.708
<b>even when you no longer have your position,</b>

176
00:10:39.708 --> 00:10:43.583
<b>when the power of that position is gone?</b>

177
00:10:43.583 --> 00:10:46.375
<b>Think about it. </b>

178
00:10:46.375 --> 00:10:50.708
<b>Do they respect your experience, </b>

179
00:10:50.708 --> 00:10:52.750
<b>do they respect you, </b>

180
00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:58.041
<b>or only the chair you sit on?</b>

181
00:10:58.041 --> 00:11:02.666
<b>The chair will change its master. </b>

182
00:11:02.666 --> 00:11:07.208
<b>The power of position will also fade.</b>

183
00:11:07.208 --> 00:11:08.791
<b>But </b>

184
00:11:08.791 --> 00:11:14.375
<b>if you work with your colleagues</b>
<b>with respect, not ego... </b>

185
00:11:14.375 --> 00:11:18.250
<b>with inspiration, not force, </b>

186
00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:23.833
<b>they will respect you today</b>
<b>and in the future as well.</b>

187
00:11:23.833 --> 00:11:27.750
<b>To lead, you don't need a big position, </b>

188
00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:28.750
<b>but</b>

189
00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:33.333
<b>a selfless spirit to understand people, </b>

190
00:11:33.333 --> 00:11:38.500
<b>to unite them with a purpose.</b>

